Ticket #4471 does not describe one problem. Subject-only deduplication merged reports from two
separate failures. The report count below is computed from unique report IDs because the ticket
export contains overlapping pages.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Problems

### Shared parser assumes month first

The shared parser reads dates as `MM/DD` for tenants whose locale is day first. This flips the day
and month for booking-v2 submissions and for app or email reports from booking-v3 tenants.

### Booking-v3 gives a month-first hint to day-first tenants

Booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People follow that hint, but the form reads the
value using the tenant's day-first locale. This is a separate form-only failure and needs its own
engineering ticket.

<Callout>
Split by computed cause, not by intake tag or subject. Intake tags are guesses, and the shared
subject is why these failures were merged.
</Callout>

The five reports the desk described as one-day moves remain with their computed cause. Tenant
locale and booking form determine the failure; the wording of an individual report does not.

